    </div>

    <p>
        For the next example we would like to vertically scroll the table. In order to achieve this
        we need to remove the border from the table. Then we need a container to provide the scroll and
        another to add the border so it looks like the scrollbars belong to the table.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong>The outer div uses <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">overflow: hidden</span> so
        the scrollbar does not draw over the border.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong>Unlike the Data Table that uses the Container header radius group the Table uses the Container content radius group
    </p>
